WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.133
-♪ She is the queen
of the moment ♪

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:08.100
♪ She is the queen
of the night ♪

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.501
♪ And she brought the heavens
and brought the light ♪

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:17.868
♪ She's the queen
of the universe ♪

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:21.000
♪ Queen of the universe ♪

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.868
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Graham Norton.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.300
That was a clip
from "Queen of the Universe."

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.400
Now, these are --
these are drag queens

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.801
on this show with great talent,

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:35.801
like, not just talent
as drag sort of connoisseurs,

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.367
but also, like, great,
really wonderful singers.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.367
-If you watch "Drag Race"
and you think,

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.667
"Mm, I like it,
but why the lip-synching?"

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.167
then this is the show for you.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:47.234
Because they sing,
and not just --

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.400
I mean, some of them
are incredible.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.734
I mean, some of them
are opera singers,

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.334
and, you know,
some of them not so much,

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.067
but it's a competition.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.501
-You know, we need --
we need some cannon fodder.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.968
So...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.033
But by the end,
they're all very good.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:03.367
-Yeah, yeah,
and it's a little fun

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.734
to watch the cannon fodder
early on.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.467
-It is great fun,
and it's one of those shows,

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.367
it's just joy.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.434
It is such a fun show.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.033
It's such a fun show
to be part of.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.434
And, you know,
it's got the panel.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.200
Mel B, Vanessa Williams,
Michelle Visage is on it,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.968
Trixie Mattel,
so it's a really fun panel.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:23.968
-And you -- So, RuPaul is
someone you met a long time ago.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.234
Did you meet here in New York?

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:28.300
-We met in New York.
I think I saw a picture.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.033
There's a -- I think I met him

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.801
at a Wigstock
a thousand years ago.

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:37.567
We have a photo, and it turns
out Ru is taller than you.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.167
-Ru is definitely
taller than me.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:40.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:43.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.868
And now, I'm --
I'm not a doctor,

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.701
but I think one of us
is aging better than the other.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.968
-Let's leave that
to the doctors, Graham.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:57.100
-Unchanged.
Untouched by time.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.033
Meanwhile -- Jesus.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.501
-It's like you guys
made a deal where you're like,

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.334
"I'll take the years
for both of us."

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.934
-Yeah, it's my gift to drag.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:10.434
-But did you do some drag
early on in your career?

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.701
-Oh, well, my --
This is weird.

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:13.868
The first thing I ever did --

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.133
There's a big, long story
behind it.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.834
But the first thing
I ever did in comedy

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.734
was a one-person show

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:22.200
called "Mother Teresa of
Calcutta's Grand Farewell Tour."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.834
And I played --
I played Mother Teresa

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.000
draped in Irish linen
tea towels.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.701
And she spoke
with an Irish accent,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.601
which, weirdly, is true,

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:34.634
because she learned her English
from some nuns in Dublin.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:35.701
-Oh, my goodness.
-I know.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:36.934
Fun fact.
Write that down.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:39.467
You won't remember it
in the morning.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:42.834
And that was my first thing.
So it wasn't really drag.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:45.100
-Yeah, it didn't seem
like you were putting the
full effort into it.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.133
-No, I really, really wasn't.
Yeah.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.133
-Do you like --
Have you met over the years,

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.534
any drag names come across?

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.267
Any drag names you like
more than others?

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.667
-I mean, the drag names I like
are just the rude ones.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.067
-The really offensive.
-I mean really terrible.

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:00.300
I mean really offensive.
This may be beeped, but...

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.434
So there was one
drag queen I met,

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.734
and everyone
just called her Anna.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.901
Anna -- This is
the drag queen Anna.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.167
And then when she went onstage,

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.801
they introduced her with
her full name, Ann Abortion.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.467
Oddly --

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.067
Oddly, in Tennessee,
she's now banned twice.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.467
-Yeah, she can't do it.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.501
I think it's like two negatives.
It makes a positive.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.133
-Yeah. She's back.
-She's actually thriving, yeah.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.400
That's a really --
That's a good one.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.968
-I mean, another --

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.968
I mean, I like the way
that drag queens

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.667
don't think things through.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:34.801
-So they just know there's got
to be a woman's name in it

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:38.200
and then a funny play
on words in the second bit.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.267
So da-da-da.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.501
So there was a drag queen
in New York

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:44.868
who thought it was a good idea
to call themselves Holly Caust.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:45.901
-Oh, boy.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.934
-And then someone
explained to her --

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.868
'cause she was going,
"I don't get many gigs.

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.834
I'm not working as much
as I thought I would."

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:55.467
And they go,
"Do you think it's the name?

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.033
Do you think it's the name?"
And she went, "Oh, okay."

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.367
And just changed it
to Holly Days.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:00.634
-And there you go.
-There you go.

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:01.901
-And now bounced right back.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.033
-Yeah. Working all the time now.
Yeah.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.834
-You're also doing Eurovision.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.133
I feel like this is --
[ Audience cheering ]

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:10.133
There we go. Some.
I'm glad.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.767
Definitely getting
a foothold here.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:15.133
-This year, it's in the U.K.
-Okay.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.601
-It hasn't been
in the U.K. for 25 years.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:19.534
I mean, we didn't win
or anything, but we've got it.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.734
-Yeah.
-And so the excitement

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:25.234
in Britain is fever pitch.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.334
King Charles and --

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:28.634
Is she Queen Camilla?
I don't know what she is.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:32.200
Anyway, they were
in Liverpool yesterday

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.234
to sort of launch
the whole thing,

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.734
and when I leave here,
I'm going back to Liverpool

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.234
'cause I'm hosting the thing,
yeah.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.667
-And do you watch -- do you
sort of watch from onstage?

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.601
Where are you
during the performance?

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:46.801
-So normally,
I'm way up in the rafters.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.400
You know,
and I can say whatever I like

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.834
because I'm never going to
meet these people.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.133
-Sure, of course.

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:55.133
-This year I'm half that person,
but I'm also onstage.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.334
-Oh, I see.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.567
-So I will be backstage
bumping into these acts.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.100
-Yeah.
-And you know someone rings them

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.801
the minute I say something
horrible about them.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.467
Someone's watching going --
-Oh, I see. Right.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:05.834
So you can't
go up in the rafters

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:07.434
and think it won't
find its way back down.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.367
-It'll find its way
back to them, yeah.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:11.734
So this year I have to be
a bit more careful.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:14.534
And also, I can't laugh at the
terrible production this year

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:15.734
because we're doing it.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:16.934
-Yeah, there you go.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.467
Oh, right,
'cause it's usually --

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:21.033
-Yeah, normally you got to go,
"These hosts are terrible."

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.767
And then it's me.
Yeah.

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.634
-Well, let me tell you,
as hosts go,

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:26.801
I look up to you a great deal.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.367
What a thrill to have
you here in person.

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:29.767
-Well, I'm thrilled to be here.
Lovely.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.234
Thank you so much. Take care.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.467
-Graham Norton.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.801
Second season
of "Queen of the Universe"

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.567
will premiere on June 2nd
on Paramount+.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:37.968
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

